  "question": {
    "text": "A molecule with the formula \\(\\mathrm{AX}_4 \\mathrm{Y}\\) has all it's elements from p-block. Element A is rarest, monoatomic, non-radioactive from its group and has the lowest ionization enthalpy value among A, X and Y. Elements X and Y have first and second highest electronegativity values respectively among all the known elements. The shape of the molecule is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
